From eac28d1dae312d33b856253c35444fdf0918e00f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:19:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: expose max bpc, Broadcast RGB and color format on
 HDMI and DP

KDE's display settings (and any DRM client) set output colour through
the DRM core's generic connector properties. nvidia-drm offered none of
them, so the colour depth the display could take could not be chosen.

On HDMI and DP connectors attach, where the kernel has the helper
(the conftests of the first commit): "max bpc" (8 to 16),
"Broadcast RGB" and "color format" (RGB, YCbCr 4:4:4, YCbCr 4:2:2).

 - nvkms-kapi: NvKmsKapiHeadModeSetConfig gets outputColor (bpc, range,
   format) with the new enums NvKmsKapiOutputColorRange/Format, and a
   head's outputColorChanged flag, which forces a modeset like a mode
   change; NvKmsKapiDynamicDisplayParams gets maxBpc, the highest depth
   the display takes in RGB, YCbCr 4:4:4 and 4:2:2 (0: unsupported),
   filled from NVKMS's supportedOutputColorFormats. NvKmsKapi
   RequestedModeSetConfigToKms() maps them onto the NVKMS head request
   (colorBpc, colorRange, colorFormat, each with its Specified flag).
 - nvidia-drm: the detect path stores maxBpc in the connector;
   nv_drm_connector_output_color() builds the head's outputColor from the
   connector state. "max bpc" is a ceiling: below what the display takes
   in the chosen format it becomes the highest depth at or under it
   (12, 10, 8 or 6), otherwise NVKMS chooses, up to the display's best
   and the max_output_color_depth parameter. Changes of "max bpc",
   "Broadcast RGB" and "color format" set outputColorChanged.
 - The hdmi.broadcast_rgb and color_format connector-state fields are
   used only where their conftests are present (kernel 7.3 has them).

Recovered from the NVIDIA module source that was installed on Daniel's
machine on 2026-10-01 (overlay /K3D/temp/stereo3d-install/nvidia-new,
never committed). Verified then: the module built for 7.3.0-rc1-stereo3d
and ran on the RTX 3060, where the KDL-46EX725 reported 12 bit
(sparky-stereo-os docs/first-runs/kwin-2026-10-01 README, 2026-10-01 03:11). The README records no
test of the individual properties.

Assisted-by: claude-sonnet (Claude Code subagent)
